        "solution_explanation": "Answer C is correct. Firms should add securities to a restricted list when the firm \nhas or may have material nonpublic information. By adding these securities to \nthis list, Andrews would uphold this standard. Because waiting until the next day \nwill not ensure that news of the merger is made public, answer A is incorrect. \nNegotiations between the two companies may take much longer, and the merger \nmay never happen. Andrews must wait until the information is disseminated to \nthe market before he trades on that information. Answer B is incorrect because \nAndrews should not disclose the information to other managers; no trading is \nallowed on material nonpublic information. \nSee Standard II(A): Material Nonpublic Information"
